0 68 246 [
[(The [tabread4~] module is suited for situations requiring more control than [tabosc4~])]
[(offers. The relationship between the two is the same as between [cos~] and [osc~],)]
[(although the units are different between [cos~] and [tabread4~]. The [cos~] object is)]
[(a cosine table and assumes an input normalized from 0 to 1 as given by [phasor~])]
[(\050although it will wrap around over this range as needed\051, while [tabread4~] takes)]
[(values from 1 to n-2 where n is the number of points in the table -- for a 131-point)]
[(table such as we have here with "waveform12", it's 1 to 129, but 129 is supposedly a)]
[(copy of 1 \050more details in the next example\051. This means it wraps at 129 to 1 \050hence,)]
[(the "good" segment is actually just 128 samples long.\051)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 69 312 [
[(The [phasor~] object generates phase ramps from 0 to 1 and repeats it at a frequency)]
[(in Hz. This is a sawtooth like signal but not a proper sawtooth waveform for synthesis)]
[(\050which is in the range of -1 to 1\051. You can use [phasor~] to drive [cos~] and)]
[([tabread4~] to implement oscillators, for instance.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
